oon-project-description-object-detection-model-for-identifying-pinnipeds-in-marine-imagery-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-pinniped-model-2-yolov11-southern-sea-otter-object-detection-model-student-sophia-mangrubang-project-description-object-detection-model-for-tracking-southern-sea-otters-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-southern-sea-otter-tracking-3-yolov12-pythias-oasis-methane-seep-benthic-megafauna-object-detection-model-student-emily-pinneo-project-description-object-detection-model-for-benthic-megafauna-at-methane-seeps-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-pythias-oasis-4-yolov11-glass-eel-object-detection-model-student-drew-rigby-project-description-object-detection-model-for-glass-eels-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-glass-eel-5-yolov11-deep-sea-coral-object-detection-model-student-taylor-meng-project-description-object-detection-and-classification-model-for-deep-sea-corals-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-coraldetectionandclassification-6-yolov11-wildfire-object-detection-model-student-roy-an-project-description-object-detection-model-for-wildfires-link-https-huggingface-co-oceancv-fire-detection-7-kmeans-segmentation-of-sea-ice-student-paige-mckay-project-description-segmentation-of-sea-ice-using-k-means-clustering-link-https-github-com-pmckay-k-means-segmentation-noaa-ice-coverage-8-kmeans-segmentation-of-marine-snow-student-victoria-dejong-project-description-segmentation-of-marine-snow-using-k-means-clustering-link-https-github-com-vdejong1927-k-means-segmentation-marine-snow","label":"Student Projects Winter 2024 This page showcases student projects from the Winter 2024 offering of OCEAN 462-C at the University of Washington. The course was taught by Ada Carter and Katie Bigham under the mentorship of Sasha Seroy. ## Projects 1. YOLOv11 Pinniped Object Detection Model - Student: Christopher Moon - Project Description: Object detection model for identifying pinnipeds in marine imagery - Link: https://huggingface.co/OceanCV/Pinniped_Model 2. YOLOv11